; ============================================================================
; AEGIS-BYZ — Autonomous Byzantine AI
; P0 native entry-point candidate
; ============================================================================
;
; PURPOSE
;   This file is the AEGIS-owned native AI entry point.
;   P0 deliberately has NO external .per dependencies.
;   It does not load AI (HD version).per, Promisory, or stock AI logic.
;
; ENGINEERING RULE
;   Architecture is represented here first. Native behavior is added only when
;   the corresponding engine primitive has been qualified for the target build.
;
; TARGET
;   AoE2DE 101.103.48987.0 / Steam BuildID 24094652
;
; ============================================================================
; AEGIS IDENTITY
; ============================================================================

(defconst aegis-entrypoint-version 1)

; ============================================================================
; RUNTIME ROOT
; ============================================================================
;
; This rule is intentionally minimal. It establishes a valid AEGIS-owned
; executable rule without importing any stock implementation.
;
(defrule
    (true)
=>
    (disable-self)
)

; ============================================================================
; WORLD MODEL
; ============================================================================
;
; Engine observations belong here conceptually. The World Model does not
; decide strategy. It records only qualified observations required by AEGIS.
;
; Required semantic distinctions:
;   CURRENT / LAST-KNOWN / UNKNOWN / UNRESOLVED
;   observation scope
;   observation age where decision-relevant
;   selective identity
;   lifecycle state
;
; No numeric state channel is allocated in P0.

; ============================================================================
; BELIEF MODEL
; ============================================================================
;
; Converts qualified observations into bounded strategic beliefs.
; Belief is not raw world state and is not enemy intent.
;
; Mandatory cross-system envelope where applicable:
;   VALID + OWNER + GENERATION + STAGE + PAYLOAD + EVIDENCE_LEVEL
;
; No numeric state channel is allocated in P0.

; ============================================================================
; SITUATION ANALYSIS
; ============================================================================
;
; Classifies the current strategic situation from World State and Belief.
; Situation is not authorization and is not an engine command.

; ============================================================================
; OBJECTIVES
; ============================================================================
;
; Converts material situations into explicit strategic objectives.
; Objective demand is not a production order and not execution authority.

; ============================================================================
; PLANNING
; ============================================================================
;
; Generates feasible capability responses to active objectives.
; Hard feasibility precedes soft evaluation.

; ============================================================================
; DECISION
; ============================================================================
;
; Selects among feasible alternatives according to explicit policy.
; Rule order must never accidentally become undocumented optimization policy.

; ============================================================================
; COMMITMENT
; ============================================================================
;
; Owns consequential strategic commitment state.
; Commitment requires explicit owner, generation, stage, and validity semantics.
; A resource reservation is not itself execution authority.

; ============================================================================
; EXECUTION
; ============================================================================
;
; Sole consequential command authority for AEGIS capabilities.
; Command issuance is recorded as ISSUED, never silently upgraded to success.

; ============================================================================
; VERIFICATION
; ============================================================================
;
; Verifies world postconditions independently of command issuance.
; Evidence ladder:
;   INTENTION -> AUTHORIZED -> ISSUED -> ACCEPTED/QUEUED -> PENDING
;   -> CREATED -> AVAILABLE -> DEPLOYED -> EFFECTIVE
;
; No evidence upgrade is implicit.

; ============================================================================
; RECOVERY / RE-ARBITRATION
; ============================================================================
;
; Failed, contradicted, superseded, or stale execution evidence returns to
; controlled arbitration. Failure does not imply blind retry.

; ============================================================================
; RESOURCE PORTFOLIO
; ============================================================================
;
; Tracks resource availability, reservations, and discretionary capacity.
; Affordability is not a guaranteed queue slot.

; ============================================================================
; PRODUCTION CAPACITY
; ============================================================================
;
; Represents production capability and availability separately from demand.
; A capability deficit is derived state, not strategic success.

; ============================================================================
; FORCE COMPOSITION
; ============================================================================
;
; Converts capability requirements into force requirements and preserves
; required mass separately from current and surplus capability.

; ============================================================================
; PRODUCTION / ECONOMIC CONVERSION
; ============================================================================
;
; Converts authorized capability requirements into executable production
; decisions after feasibility, resource, and arbitration checks.

; ============================================================================
; FIRST VERTICAL SLICE
; ============================================================================
;
; Cavalry Threat Containment:
;   OBSERVE ENEMY
;       -> CLASSIFY CAVALRY THREAT
;       -> DEFINE CAMEL REQUIREMENT
;       -> CHECK CAPABILITY / RESOURCES
;       -> SELECT PRODUCER
;       -> COMMIT
;       -> EXECUTE
;       -> VERIFY
;       -> RECOVER / RE-ARBITRATE
;       -> REASSESS
;
; ============================================================================
; P0 BOUNDARY
; ============================================================================
;
; This entry point intentionally proves only package ownership and native
; entry-point structure. It does not pretend that unqualified ABI semantics
; are already runtime-proven.
;
; End of AEGIS-BYZ P0 entry point.
